      {
        "id": 99302,
        "name": "phantaskippy",
        "username": "phantaskippy",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-04-15T15:30:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I did the 30-min. demo twice, and I loved it.</p><p>It was against the Technovores, and he cut the shields on the enemy ships by 2, and that there were fewer enemy ships than there should have been, other than that I don't know any specific changes.</p><p>Unfortunately I have a limited group to play with, and they didn't like GSF, although I think they would have if we had played it earlier in the weekend, Sunday we were mostly just tired, cranky and ready to go home.</p><p>The demo doesn't get to show off the deckbuilding strategy, (since you go through your deck 1-2 times) but it certainly shows off GSF's ridiculous comboing, which was a lot of fun, both games involved most players doing something awesome.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>It wasn't a Pax purchase for me, but it is on the list of games I need to get. &nbsp;If I had a group to play it with regularly it would have been bought on the spot.</p>",
        "post_number": 4,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:27:14.014Z",
